Subject: [PATCH] avcodec: offer AV1 Main8 monochrome to V4L2 Request

Offer DRM_PRIME for Main-profile GRAY8 input, leaving NVDEC, 4:2:0
selection and non-Main profiles unchanged. Native SC2 qualification
observed complete original luma and hardware-generated neutral128 UV
in the existing NV12 export, including reference reuse and teardown.

Keep Main10 monochrome unexposed: its reconstructed luma is correct,
but the tested FBC payload explicitly contains128 chroma instead of
neutral512. Do not relabel that surface, synthesize UV on the CPU or
change the source bitstream. The native admission guard remains.

The Request path already preserves MONO_CHROME and sequence bit depth.
Keep existing capture negotiation and truthful DRM descriptors unchanged.

--- a/libavcodec/av1dec.c
+++ b/libavcodec/av1dec.c
@@ -557,4 +557,8 @@
 #if CONFIG_AV1_NVDEC_HWACCEL
         *fmtp++ = AV_PIX_FMT_CUDA;
 #endif
+#if CONFIG_AV1_V4L2REQUEST_HWACCEL
+        if (seq->seq_profile == FF_PROFILE_AV1_MAIN)
+            *fmtp++ = AV_PIX_FMT_DRM_PRIME;
+#endif
         break;
